Deep Learning Module – Question Bank - Batch 1

1. Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs) – 15 Questions

1. What is an epoch in deep learning?
A) One forward pass of all training data
B) One backward pass of all training data
C) One complete cycle of forward and backward pass
D) A single neuron activation

(Answer: C)

2. In a neural network, what connects the neurons of one layer to the next?
A) Bias
B) Activation Function
C) Weights
D) Loss Function

(Answer: C)

3. What is the primary reason for using multiple hidden layers in a neural network?
A) To increase training time
B) To capture complex patterns and features
C) To reduce the number of parameters
D) To prevent overfitting

(Answer: B)

4. What is the objective of a loss function in a neural network?
A) Maximize accuracy
B) Minimize error
C) Optimize learning rate
D) Adjust neurons

(Answer: B)

5. Which of the following is a challenge with gradient descent?
A) Model generalization
B) Vanishing Gradient Problem
C) Improved accuracy
D) Fast convergence

(Answer: B)

6. Which optimizer is commonly used in deep learning due to its adaptive learning rate?
A) SGD (Stochastic Gradient Descent)
B) Adam
C) RMSprop
D) Momentum

(Answer: B)

7. What is backpropagation used for in neural networks?
A) To move data backward through the network
B) To calculate and update weights using gradients
C) To initialize neural network weights
D) To reduce model complexity

(Answer: B)

8. Which type of layer is responsible for feature extraction in a CNN?
A) Dense Layer
B) Convolutional Layer
C) Pooling Layer
D) Activation Layer

(Answer: B)

9. What is the purpose of the MaxPooling layer in CNNs?
A) To extract important features and reduce dimensions
B) To add more convolution filters
C) To perform normalization
D) To apply activation functions

(Answer: A)

10. Which filter size is typically preferred to capture fine image details?
A) 1×1
B) 3×3
C) 5×5
D) 7×7

(Answer: B)

11. In a CNN, what does a higher number of filters in a convolutional layer typically achieve?
A) Faster training time
B) Reduced model complexity
C) Learning more features
D) Reduced memory usage

(Answer: C)

12. Which of the following is a commonly used image classification model for Transfer Learning?
A) AlexNet
B) GPT-4
C) RNN
D) DBSCAN

(Answer: A)

13. Why is Transfer Learning beneficial for small datasets?
A) It reduces the number of parameters
B) It requires less computation
C) It uses knowledge from pretrained models to extract useful features
D) It uses unsupervised learning techniques

(Answer: C)

14. Which activation function is commonly used in the output layer for binary face mask detection?
A) Sigmoid
B) ReLU
C) Tanh
D) Softmax

(Answer: A)

15. In face mask detection, what is a good technique to reduce false positives?
A) Increase the number of pooling layers
B) Apply data augmentation
C) Reduce the number of convolution layers
D) Use a linear activation function

(Answer: B)
